317 - Lead Me to Calvary
 / 
Key: Db
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 317
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[Db/Ab]King of my life, I crown [Ebm/Bb]Thee now, [Db/Ab]Thine shall [Gb]the glory [Db/Ab]be;
[Ab]Lest I forget [Db/Ab]Thy thorn crowned brow, Lead me to Calvary.
[Gb]Lest I forget [Fm]Gethsemane, [Db/Ab]Lest I forget Thine [Ebm/Gb]agony;
[Ab]Lest I forget [Ab7]Thy love for me, [Db/Ab]Lead [Ab]me to Calvary.

Refrain:
[Db]Lest I forget [Ab7]Gethsemane,
[Bbm]Lest I forget [Am]Thine [Bbm]agony;
[Db/Ab]Lest I forget Thy love for [Ebm/Gb]me,
[Db/F]Lead me to Calvary.

Verse 2:
[Db/Ab]Show me the tomb [Ebm/Bb]where [Db/Ab]Thou [Gb]wast [Ab]laid,
[Ab]Tenderly [Db/Ab]mourned and wept;
[Gb]Angels [Fm]in [Db/Ab]robes of light [Ebm/Gb]arrayed
[Ab]Guarded [Ab7]Thee whilst [Ab]Thou slept.

Verse 3:
[Db/Ab]Let me like Mary, through [Gb]the [Ab]gloom,
[Ab]Come [Db/Ab]with a gift to Thee;
[Gb]Show to [Fm]me [Db/Ab]now the empty [Ebm/Gb]tomb,
[Ab]Lead me [Ab7]to Calvary.

Verse 4:
[Db/Ab]May I be willing, Lord, [Gb]to [Ab]bear
[Ab]Daily [Db/Ab]my cross for Thee;
[Gb]Even [Fm]Thy [Db/Ab]cup of grief to [Ebm/Gb]share,
[Ab]Thou hast [Ab7]borne all [Ab]for me.
